(5646748, 820923, 24454, '<td valign="top">Richard, I saw this on the forums, so I won''t be voting on it, but I have to say, from what I''ve seen, if this doesn''t win a ribbon, you will have been totally robbed!  I don''t think that lake has ever looked more breathtaking!  Bravo!!! . . . .<br/> <br/>. . . . I''m back after just having finished voting.  Yep!  This one most DEFINITELY deserves blue!  I love how it is so elegantly NOT overdone, yet each tone and color is exquisitely separate and beautiful!  This needs to be the HDR poster photo!  Maybe you can teach some of the others how to do it :)<br/> <br/>Congratulations!</td>', 'Richard, I saw this on the forums, so I won''t be voting on it, but I have to say, from what I''ve seen, if this doesn''t win a ribbon, you will have been totally robbed!  I don''t think that lake has ever looked more breathtaking!  Bravo!!! . . . . . . . . I''m back after just having finished voting.  Yep!  This one most DEFINITELY deserves blue!  I love how it is so elegantly NOT overdone, yet each tone and color is exquisitely separate and beautiful!  This needs to be the HDR poster photo!  Maybe you can teach some of the others how to do it :) Congratulations!', '2009-09-14 15:22:55.000000', NULL, 1),
