(5647527, 820923, 54645, '<td valign="top">This is stunning. Clearly a top 5 image. Somewhat restrained use of HDR which I like. To nit pick the processing, I wonder what could be done with the trees top left that are back lit. 9</td>', 'This is stunning. Clearly a top 5 image. Somewhat restrained use of HDR which I like. To nit pick the processing, I wonder what could be done with the trees top left that are back lit. 9', '2009-09-15 03:35:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647534, 820860, 106806, '<td valign="top">a little too green for my personal taste, nevertheless a nicely taken shot.....  mind you taken in early early fall/autumn when the leaves are just turning the trees would also then look a bit rusty marking the passage of years.</td>', 'a little too green for my personal taste, nevertheless a nicely taken shot.....  mind you taken in early early fall/autumn when the leaves are just turning the trees would also then look a bit rusty marking the passage of years.', '2009-09-15 03:51:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647536, 820963, 106806, '<td valign="top">*sigh* why do I like modern horrible buildings soooo much. I love the way you''ve brought the texture out in the white facia. I''d love to know how the picture would fair with a more pronounced silver hue to the non-ground windows and a more golden hue to the ground.</td>', '*sigh* why do I like modern horrible buildings soooo much. I love the way you''ve brought the texture out in the white facia. I''d love to know how the picture would fair with a more pronounced silver hue to the non-ground windows and a more golden hue to the ground.', '2009-09-15 03:59:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647537, 820425, 106806, '<td valign="top">another reason why some folks don''t like HDR. I''m reminded of those picutures that have animated waterfalls and pizo electric speaker in the back playing bird song. But hey this is HDR challange and the detail in this photo is great, plenty to look at.</td>', 'another reason why some folks don''t like HDR. I''m reminded of those picutures that have animated waterfalls and pizo electric speaker in the back playing bird song. But hey this is HDR challange and the detail in this photo is great, plenty to look at.', '2009-09-15 04:01:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647538, 820838, 106806, '<td valign="top">An example of why some folk love HDR. The detailing in the roof really makes this photo.</td>', 'An example of why some folk love HDR. The detailing in the roof really makes this photo.', '2009-09-15 04:08:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647540, 821094, 106806, '<td valign="top">don''t think your''e gonna need anyone to say how well done this is. Classic.</td>', 'don''t think your''e gonna need anyone to say how well done this is. Classic.', '2009-09-15 04:11:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647544, 821078, 86628, '<td valign="top">I may be wrong, but I don''t see the point of using HDR for this.  The scene seems to have low dynamic range, so this may as well have been a "normal" capture.  That said, this is still my highest rated image of the challenge - it is simply a stunning photo.</td>', 'I may be wrong, but I don''t see the point of using HDR for this.  The scene seems to have low dynamic range, so this may as well have been a "normal" capture.  That said, this is still my highest rated image of the challenge - it is simply a stunning photo.', '2009-09-15 05:00:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647549, 820686, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like the contrast of the yellow lights with the blue sky and water. Of course, the exposure method does nice stuff for the flowing water. The stereotypical "HDR look" is visible, but restrained.</td>', 'I like the contrast of the yellow lights with the blue sky and water. Of course, the exposure method does nice stuff for the flowing water. The stereotypical "HDR look" is visible, but restrained.', '2009-09-15 05:17:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647550, 820941, 83313, '<td valign="top">Great tones this brought out. It really glows. Composition seems a bit more shoved over than is my preference, I assume you were wanting to not leave out that gorgeous sky.</td>', 'Great tones this brought out. It really glows. Composition seems a bit more shoved over than is my preference, I assume you were wanting to not leave out that gorgeous sky.', '2009-09-15 05:19:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647551, 820964, 83313, '<td valign="top">Too weird. I''m not caring for the treatment of this, but I want to make it clear that it''s not bad, just personal taste. Are those headphone wires? I''ll bet that pot does some interesting things for audio enhancement. You do get a vote on the positive side just for the sheer absurdity of this, however!</td>', 'Too weird. I''m not caring for the treatment of this, but I want to make it clear that it''s not bad, just personal taste. Are those headphone wires? I''ll bet that pot does some interesting things for audio enhancement. You do get a vote on the positive side just for the sheer absurdity of this, however!', '2009-09-15 05:23:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647552, 821036, 83313, '<td valign="top">A realistic and effective use of HDR to show all the details in this. As an artistic piece of photography, I''m not caring much for the composition of the scene. The tunnel entry being cut off at the top seems a problem to me, and I think overall the comp could have been done from a more interesting perspective. Again, you did great on the actual usage of HDR and I have to give you a positive vote for that.</td>', 'A realistic and effective use of HDR to show all the details in this. As an artistic piece of photography, I''m not caring much for the composition of the scene. The tunnel entry being cut off at the top seems a problem to me, and I think overall the comp could have been done from a more interesting perspective. Again, you did great on the actual usage of HDR and I have to give you a positive vote for that.', '2009-09-15 05:27:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647553, 820991, 83313, '<td valign="top">Composition seems a bit too centered to me, and the scene itself does not stand out, I''m afraid. The moderate use of some HDR or tonemapping treatment does help the retro appearance of this place.</td>', 'Composition seems a bit too centered to me, and the scene itself does not stand out, I''m afraid. The moderate use of some HDR or tonemapping treatment does help the retro appearance of this place.', '2009-09-15 05:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647554, 820963, 83313, '<td valign="top">Good enough, but not impacting me any. My own preference with using HDR and modern buildings is when the treatment helps to give it a clean and bold appearance. In this case it seems to muddy the whites some. Blue sky could use a little noise reduction.</td>', 'Good enough, but not impacting me any. My own preference with using HDR and modern buildings is when the treatment helps to give it a clean and bold appearance. In this case it seems to muddy the whites some. Blue sky could use a little noise reduction.', '2009-09-15 05:33:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647555, 820692, 83313, '<td valign="top">Fairly sure this is not a multiple exposure HDR, (Set up a tripod in the car and stopped it at the top of the climb?) but the effect works well, regardless of how it was accomplished.</td>', 'Fairly sure this is not a multiple exposure HDR, (Set up a tripod in the car and stopped it at the top of the climb?) but the effect works well, regardless of how it was accomplished.', '2009-09-15 05:35:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647556, 820829, 83313, '<td valign="top">Excellent use of HDR to give a realistic look with extra detail, and a great choice of subject.</td>', 'Excellent use of HDR to give a realistic look with extra detail, and a great choice of subject.', '2009-09-15 05:36:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647557, 820983, 83313, '<td valign="top">Of course, I love these old rusty-crusties. The blue just pops off the screen at me.</td>', 'Of course, I love these old rusty-crusties. The blue just pops off the screen at me.', '2009-09-15 05:37:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647560, 820509, 83313, '<td valign="top">The treatment works wonderfully on all the fine details, and brings out the subtle play of the lighting.</td>', 'The treatment works wonderfully on all the fine details, and brings out the subtle play of the lighting.', '2009-09-15 05:38:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647563, 820518, 83313, '<td valign="top">A good traditional use of HDR for a landscape. S''nice.</td>', 'A good traditional use of HDR for a landscape. S''nice.', '2009-09-15 05:39:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647565, 821017, 83313, '<td valign="top">The photo most certainly fits the title. Not sure it''s wowing me much, but I don''t think that was the intention here. Bit of a busy scene in the background, but a good capture of a moment that is different from the usual wedding photo. I was going to give it a 5, but the more I look at it, the more I appreciate it and I think it deserves a positive side vote.</td>', 'The photo most certainly fits the title. Not sure it''s wowing me much, but I don''t think that was the intention here. Bit of a busy scene in the background, but a good capture of a moment that is different from the usual wedding photo. I was going to give it a 5, but the more I look at it, the more I appreciate it and I think it deserves a positive side vote.', '2009-09-15 05:43:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647566, 821097, 28322, '<td valign="top">Wonderful by all means, love it, 10</td>', 'Wonderful by all means, love it, 10', '2009-09-15 05:45:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647568, 821098, 83313, '<td valign="top">The stereotypical "HDR look" is very strong here. (Duh). I like it. Of course, the sky is fantastic, but you knew that already.</td>', 'The stereotypical "HDR look" is very strong here. (Duh). I like it. Of course, the sky is fantastic, but you knew that already.', '2009-09-15 05:48:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647569, 820923, 28322, '<td valign="top">This should Rib, I''d say Top 3 '''' if you survived me :P '''' Just kidding, it is amazing and can''t think of anything that would improve it, top of the line photography, the one that you''d love to hand on your wall, even then, it would still look too good to be true, very well done, 10</td>', 'This should Rib, I''d say Top 3 '''' if you survived me :P '''' Just kidding, it is amazing and can''t think of anything that would improve it, top of the line photography, the one that you''d love to hand on your wall, even then, it would still look too good to be true, very well done, 10', '2009-09-15 05:48:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647571, 821012, 28322, '<td valign="top">Glad you mentioned it is 3 shot HDR '''' a secret .. I hate 1 shot HDR '''', love the feeling of the image, how peaceful it look, how a group of people would meet to do something they all love to do, like photography, a very well deserved 10. <br/>Cheers,</td>', 'Glad you mentioned it is 3 shot HDR '''' a secret .. I hate 1 shot HDR '''', love the feeling of the image, how peaceful it look, how a group of people would meet to do something they all love to do, like photography, a very well deserved 10. Cheers,', '2009-09-15 05:50:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647572, 820996, 83313, '<td valign="top">What an unusual sculpture! Reminds me a little of a waterslide, or some contrived challenge on a Japanese game show. At least I hope it''s not a waterslide, those round things half way down could really hurt!</td>', 'What an unusual sculpture! Reminds me a little of a waterslide, or some contrived challenge on a Japanese game show. At least I hope it''s not a waterslide, those round things half way down could really hurt!', '2009-09-15 05:50:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647573, 820729, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nice use of nighttime colors for this. The clean lines and tones of the bridge really stand out to me. The sky seems a bit grainy and I wonder if some selective NR or blur could help that aspect a little.</td>', 'Nice use of nighttime colors for this. The clean lines and tones of the bridge really stand out to me. The sky seems a bit grainy and I wonder if some selective NR or blur could help that aspect a little.', '2009-09-15 05:53:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647575, 820373, 83313, '<td valign="top">Great use of the effect to enhance a b/w, but why is the nose of the car cut off at the edge of the frame? You might get some flak for the overhead wires showing as well. I''m on the fence as to whether they work for the scene or not. I''d love to see some other perspectives of this if you have any to post in the outtakes thread afterwards.</td>', 'Great use of the effect to enhance a b/w, but why is the nose of the car cut off at the edge of the frame? You might get some flak for the overhead wires showing as well. I''m on the fence as to whether they work for the scene or not. I''d love to see some other perspectives of this if you have any to post in the outtakes thread afterwards.', '2009-09-15 05:56:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647590, 820732, 96574, '<td valign="top">it''s too oversaturated and OOF for me</td>', 'it''s too oversaturated and OOF for me', '2009-09-15 06:51:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5647591, 820965, 99695, '<td valign="top">You can clone out the electricity pole in advanced editing. I think it would be better for the composition. Also some more contrast might help.</td>', 'You can clone out the electricity pole in advanced editing. I think it would be better for the composition. Also some more contrast might help.', '2009-09-15 06:52:20.000000', NULL, 1),
