(5656394, 820513, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>The composition and colours of this shot are good, however, the processing has left it looking very flat and unnatural... there''s also a little too much going on above and behind the main flower which distracts the viewer away from the main subject.</td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  The composition and colours of this shot are good, however, the processing has left it looking very flat and unnatural... there''s also a little too much going on above and behind the main flower which distracts the viewer away from the main subject.', '2009-09-21 20:50:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656398, 821078, 109174, '<td valign="top">Excellent work<br/> <br/>Nasa</td>', 'Excellent work Nasa', '2009-09-21 20:55:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656399, 821006, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>I think the biggest issue with this image is the centred composition... that and the fact that it doesn''t look HDR enough perhaps, though your faux-HDR processing did a decent job of giving the clouds a HDRish feel.  I''d ask you not to give up on HDR... I think there''s a lot of good Team Suck and the like could do, artistically, with HDR.</td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  I think the biggest issue with this image is the centred composition... that and the fact that it doesn''t look HDR enough perhaps, though your faux-HDR processing did a decent job of giving the clouds a HDRish feel.  I''d ask you not to give up on HDR... I think there''s a lot of good Team Suck and the like could do, artistically, with HDR.', '2009-09-21 20:55:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656404, 821000, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>Great capture, and given the right challenge, this would have fair a lot better, but this doesn''t lend itself to HDR (IMO).  Colours are a little flat, and while I rate it as one of the images features, the lens flare probably hurt your score in the end too.  Oh... also could have cropped just a tab more off the bottom to lose the white bit in the bottom right.</td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  Great capture, and given the right challenge, this would have fair a lot better, but this doesn''t lend itself to HDR (IMO).  Colours are a little flat, and while I rate it as one of the images features, the lens flare probably hurt your score in the end too.  Oh... also could have cropped just a tab more off the bottom to lose the white bit in the bottom right.', '2009-09-21 20:59:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656405, 820932, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>A good image.  A little over saturated for my liking and I think it might have done better in voting with a tighter crop (top and bottom).  Details are good, and you''ve the details in the smoke are brilliant.</td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  A good image.  A little over saturated for my liking and I think it might have done better in voting with a tighter crop (top and bottom).  Details are good, and you''ve the details in the smoke are brilliant.', '2009-09-21 21:03:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656415, 820988, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>First... welcome back to the fold after serving your suspension... <br/> <br/>A good capture, however, I think you''ve tried too hard to make it look like HDR... the overstauration, the haloing, the black grittiness... while all these are characteristics associated with HDR, they''re not things that improve the image.  I think there''s stuff HDR processing can bring to an image w/o having to adopt these HDR cliche elements (IMO).</td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  First... welcome back to the fold after serving your suspension...  A good capture, however, I think you''ve tried too hard to make it look like HDR... the overstauration, the haloing, the black grittiness... while all these are characteristics associated with HDR, they''re not things that improve the image.  I think there''s stuff HDR processing can bring to an image w/o having to adopt these HDR cliche elements (IMO).', '2009-09-21 21:10:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656420, 820941, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>Very nice image, and another good example of how to use HDR for good, and not evil, in that your image has benefited from the increase dynamic range w/o adopting all the usual HDR cliches of haloing, black clouds/skys, grittiness etc.<br/> <br/>I love the detail, colour and composition.  Well done.</td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  Very nice image, and another good example of how to use HDR for good, and not evil, in that your image has benefited from the increase dynamic range w/o adopting all the usual HDR cliches of haloing, black clouds/skys, grittiness etc. I love the detail, colour and composition.  Well done.', '2009-09-21 21:15:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656427, 820323, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>This is a stunning image and really deserves to have finished higher (IMO).  It''s yet another example from the Team Suck how to do HDR well... how to use the technique without overdoing it.  Details and colours are brilliant.</td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  This is a stunning image and really deserves to have finished higher (IMO).  It''s yet another example from the Team Suck how to do HDR well... how to use the technique without overdoing it.  Details and colours are brilliant.', '2009-09-21 21:19:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656438, 820715, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>Good use of HDR to get detail in the windons, facade and some of the sky, however, the colours are a tad flat and there''s not enough pull to any point of interest in the image, so one''s eyes just wander the image.</td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  Good use of HDR to get detail in the windons, facade and some of the sky, however, the colours are a tad flat and there''s not enough pull to any point of interest in the image, so one''s eyes just wander the image.', '2009-09-21 21:22:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656457, 820096, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>Well and truly overprocessed, but you already know that.  Putting that aside, I think this image had some great potential for HDR (especially those clouds), though, I think you''ve cropped a little too tight on the right.<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-09-21 20:26:25.</i></td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  Well and truly overprocessed, but you already know that.  Putting that aside, I think this image had some great potential for HDR (especially those clouds), though, I think you''ve cropped a little too tight on the right. ', '2009-09-21 21:25:43.000000', '2009-09-21 21:26:25.000000', 0),
(5656471, 820692, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>Nice image.  Brilliant location.  Composition is good, and you''ve done well with the HDR processing, however, the bottom left (the trees) is still too dark, and the haloing at the top of the rollercoaster on the right is an unfortunate by product of HDR which I''d try to avoid (I know it''s easier said than done).  Also, the colours in the sky look a tad flat... a result of noise reduction perhaps... <br/> <br/>All that said... this is a good shot, and a worthy addition to your profile page.</td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  Nice image.  Brilliant location.  Composition is good, and you''ve done well with the HDR processing, however, the bottom left (the trees) is still too dark, and the haloing at the top of the rollercoaster on the right is an unfortunate by product of HDR which I''d try to avoid (I know it''s easier said than done).  Also, the colours in the sky look a tad flat... a result of noise reduction perhaps...  All that said... this is a good shot, and a worthy addition to your profile page.', '2009-09-21 21:34:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656472, 820995, 32011, '<td valign="top">Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties... <br/> <br/>I''m surprised that this didn''t do better with the voters.  It''s perhaps a little over done with the HDR processing (haloing and too much black), and... is that crane really tilting that much... rather unsettling.</td>', 'Commenting as part of my Team Suck duties...  I''m surprised that this didn''t do better with the voters.  It''s perhaps a little over done with the HDR processing (haloing and too much black), and... is that crane really tilting that much... rather unsettling.', '2009-09-21 21:37:43.000000', NULL, 0),
